const PUZZLES=[
{title:"The Opening Serve",section:"I. Sunrise",body:`<h3>🏐 VOLLEYBALL LOGIC</h3><p>Three teams — <span class="puzzle-highlight">Falcons</span>, <span class="puzzle-highlight">Wolves</span>, <span class="puzzle-highlight">Ravens</span> — played a round-robin (each team played 2 matches).</p><ul style="margin-left:1.5rem;line-height:2.2"><li>Falcons beat Wolves by exactly 3 points.</li><li>Ravens beat Falcons. Score: 25–21.</li><li>Wolves beat Ravens. Combined score: 47.</li><li>Most total points across both matches wins.</li></ul><p style="margin-top:0.8rem">Which team won the tournament?</p>`,answer:"ravens",hints:["Wolves vs Ravens: combined score 47. Volleyball sets go to 25. Try 25–22 (Wolves 25, Ravens 22).","Falcons beat Wolves by 3 → 25–22. Tally: Ravens=47, Falcons=46, Wolves=47.","Ravens and Wolves both 47 total. But Ravens beat Wolves head-to-head — Ravens win!"],notesRevealed:"B♭4 — D5 — F5",sectionMsg:"The sun rises. Your journey begins."},
{title:"The Brass Cipher",section:"I. Sunrise",body:`<h3>🎺 TROMBONE POSITIONS</h3><p>The trombone slide has 7 positions. Each lowers pitch by one semitone from position 1.</p><div class="code-block">2nd harmonic: 1=B♭  2=A  3=A♭  4=G  5=G♭  6=F  7=E</div><p>Decode this sequence — read <em>letter names only</em> (ignore ♭/♯):</p><div class="code-block">Sequence:  1 — 6 — 7 — 4 — 1 — 4</div><p>What six letters do they spell? (no spaces)</p>`,answer:"bfebgb",hints:["Map positions: 1=B♭, 6=F, 7=E, 4=G, 1=B♭, 4=G","Letter names only: B, F, E, G, B, G","Type the letters in order: BFEBGB"],notesRevealed:"G4 — A4 — B♭4",sectionMsg:"The melody begins to wake."},
{title:"The Traveller's Riddle",section:"I. Sunrise",body:`<h3>🌍 SPHERICAL GEOMETRY</h3><p>A traveller leaves the <span class="puzzle-highlight">City of Beginnings</span> and walks:</p><ul style="margin-left:1.5rem;line-height:2.2"><li>3 days <strong>North</strong></li><li>3 days <strong>East</strong></li><li>3 days <strong>South</strong></li><li>3 days <strong>West</strong></li></ul><p>He expects to return — but ends up <em>one day's walk away</em>. The world is a sphere.</p><p style="margin-top:0.8rem">Which direction does he now face the City of Beginnings?</p><p style="color:var(--ink-dim);font-size:0.85rem">(Answer: North, South, East, or West)</p>`,answer:"south",hints:["On a flat map this loop is perfect. On a sphere, latitude lines are shorter near poles.","Near the North Pole, '3 days East' traces a much smaller circle.","He ends up north of start — City is to his South."],notesRevealed:"C5 — D5 — E♭5",sectionMsg:"Three fragments of sunrise, revealed."},
{title:"The Grade Problem",section:"II. The Climb",body:`<h3>🧗 CLIMBING MATHEMATICS</h3><p>French grades: 5a=1, 5b=2, 5c=3, 6a=4, 6a+=5, 6b=6, 6b+=7, 6c=8, 6c+=9, 7a=10, 7a+=11…</p><table><tr><th>Route</th><th>Grade</th><th>Attempts</th></tr><tr><td>Obsidian Wall</td><td>7a</td><td>3</td></tr><tr><td>Sunfire Crack</td><td>6c+</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>The Phantom Slab</td><td>6b+</td><td>5</td></tr><tr><td>Dragon's Tooth</td><td>7a+</td><td>2</td></tr></table><p style="margin-top:0.8rem"><strong>Score = grade# × (6 − attempts)</strong>, min 0 per route. Total?</p>`,answer:"126",hints:["Grade numbers: 7a=10, 6c+=9, 6b+=7, 7a+=11","Per route: 10×3=30, 9×5=45, 7×1=7, 11×4=44","Total = 30+45+7+44 = 126"],notesRevealed:"F5 — G5 — A♭5",sectionMsg:"The climb steepens. The melody rises with you."},
{title:"The Mana Vault",section:"II. The Climb",body:`<h3>🃏 MTG — COMBAT MATH</h3><p>You are at <strong>4 life</strong>. Opponent attacks with:</p><table><tr><th>Creature</th><th>P/T</th><th>Ability</th></tr><tr><td>Goblin Guide</td><td>2/2</td><td>Haste</td></tr><tr><td>Monastery Swiftspear</td><td>1/2</td><td>Prowess (+1/+1 per noncreature spell)</td></tr><tr><td>Eidolon of the Great Revel</td><td>2/2</td><td>CMC≤3 spell → 2 damage to caster</td></tr></table><p style="margin-top:0.8rem">Opponent casts <strong>2 noncreature spells</strong>. Swiftspear becomes 3/4. Eidolon deals <strong>2 damage</strong> → you're at <strong>2 life</strong>.</p><p>Blockers: <span class="puzzle-highlight">Wall of Omens (0/4)</span> and <span class="puzzle-highlight">Llanowar Elves (1/1)</span>. Block optimally. Life total after combat?</p>`,answer:"0",hints:["Attackers: Guide 2/2, Swiftspear 3/4, Eidolon 2/2. You have 2 life, 2 blockers.","Wall blocks Swiftspear (0/4 survives). Elves block Guide (die, 0 damage). Eidolon unblocked.","Eidolon hits for 2 → 2−2 = 0. You survive at 0!"],notesRevealed:"B♭5 — C6 — B♭5",sectionMsg:"Blocked optimally. Just barely survived."},
{title:"The Recursion Forest",section:"II. The Climb",body:`<h3>💻 TRACE THE RECURSION</h3><p>What does this print when called as <code style="color:#7ee787">f(5)</code>?</p><div class="code-block">def f(n):
    if n &lt;= 0:
        return 0
    if n == 1:
        return 1
    return f(n-1) + f(n-2)

print(f(5))</div>`,answer:"5",hints:["Trace: compute f(0), f(1), f(2), f(3), f(4).","f(0)=0, f(1)=1, f(2)=1, f(3)=2, f(4)=3","f(5) = f(4)+f(3) = 3+2 = 5. Fibonacci!"],notesRevealed:"G4 — F4 — E♭4",sectionMsg:"Even code has rhythm. Section II complete."},
{title:"The Fibonacci Garden",section:"III. Game On",body:`<h3>🌿 NATURE'S HIDDEN PATTERN</h3><p>Sunflower spirals come in consecutive Fibonacci numbers. A botanist counts <strong>34 clockwise spirals</strong>. Total (CW+CCW) is under 100. Ratio larger÷smaller ≈ <strong>1.618</strong>.</p><p style="margin-top:0.8rem">How many counter-clockwise spirals?</p>`,answer:"21",hints:["Fibonacci near 34: …21, 34, 55…","34/21 ≈ 1.619 ≈ 1.618 ✓","Counter-clockwise is always the smaller. 21 < 34 → answer: 21."],notesRevealed:"D5 — C5 — B♭4",sectionMsg:"Nature hides its music well."},
{title:"The Probability Spike",section:"III. Game On",body:`<h3>📊 VOLLEYBALL STATISTICS</h3><p>Spike success rate: <strong>70%</strong> on first attempt. If he fails, fatigue drops it to <strong>40%</strong>. Max 2 attempts.</p><p style="margin-top:0.8rem">Probability of scoring (%, nearest whole number)?</p>`,answer:"82",hints:["P(scores 1st) = 0.70. P(fails 1st AND scores 2nd) = 0.30 × 0.40.","0.30 × 0.40 = 0.12","Total P = 0.70 + 0.12 = 0.82 = 82%"],notesRevealed:"A4 — G4 — F4",sectionMsg:"82% chance of brilliance. 100% earned."},
{title:"The Dead Code",section:"III. Game On",body:`<h3>💻 WHAT GETS PRINTED?</h3><div class="code-block">result = []
for i in range(10):
    if i % 2 == 0:
        if i % 3 == 0:
            result.append(i * 2)
        else:
            result.append(i)
    else:
        if i > 5:
            result.append(i * i)

print(sum(result))</div>`,answer:"156",hints:["Even & div by 3: 0,6 → 0,12. Even not div by 3: 2,4,8. Odd > 5: 7,9 → 49,81.","result = [0, 2, 4, 12, 8, 49, 81]","0+2+4+12+8+49+81 = 156"],notesRevealed:"E♭5 — F5 — G5",sectionMsg:"Section III: Game On — fully unlocked."},
{title:"The Grand Council",section:"IV. Summit",body:`<h3>🏔️ EINSTEIN LOGIC PUZZLE</h3><p>5 mountaineers, 5 peaks, 5 snacks, 5 jackets. Who climbed the <span class="puzzle-highlight">Matterhorn</span>?</p><ul style="margin-left:1.5rem;line-height:2;font-size:0.9rem"><li>The Norwegian is in position 1.</li><li>The red jacket is next to the Mont Blanc climber.</li><li>The Italian brought trail mix.</li><li>The Eiger climber is in position 3.</li><li>The green jacket brought chocolate.</li><li>The Austrian is next to the yellow jacket.</li><li>Position 3 brought nuts.</li><li>The Swiss climbed the Jungfrau.</li><li>The Norwegian is next to the blue jacket.</li><li>The energy bar person is next to the Eiger climber.</li><li>Yellow jacket summited the Zugspitze.</li><li>The German brought energy bars.</li><li>The Austrian is in position 2.</li><li>The Norwegian brought sandwiches.</li></ul><p style="margin-top:0.8rem">Answer: nationality of the Matterhorn climber.</p>`,answer:"german",hints:["Pos1=Norwegian, Pos2=Austrian, Pos3=Eiger+nuts. Norwegian next to blue → blue=Austrian.","Austrian next to yellow. German=energy bars, next to Eiger(Pos3) → German=Pos4.","Swiss=Jungfrau=Pos5. Italian=Pos3. German(Pos4) climbed Matterhorn."],notesRevealed:"B♭5 — A5 — G5",sectionMsg:"The summit is in sight."},
{title:"The Forbidden Tome",section:"IV. Summit",body:`<h3>📚 ALPHABET CIPHER</h3><p>A=1, B=2 … Z=26. Decode:</p><div class="code-block">20  18  15  13  2  15  14  5</div><p>What word do these numbers spell?</p>`,answer:"trombone",hints:["T=20. Start mapping.","20=T, 18=R, 15=O, 13=M, 2=B, 15=O, 14=N, 5=E","T-R-O-M-B-O-N-E. Your instrument. 🎺"],notesRevealed:"F5 — E♭5 — D5",sectionMsg:"You found the hidden word. It was always about the music."},
{title:"The Force of the Mountain",section:"IV. Summit",body:`<h3>⚙️ CLIMBING PHYSICS</h3><p>A <strong>70 kg</strong> climber hangs from a rope through a bolt directly above. Both rope sides hang vertically. Frictionless carabiner. g = 10 m/s².</p><p style="margin-top:0.8rem">Total force on the bolt in <strong>Newtons</strong>?</p>`,answer:"1400",hints:["Weight = 70 × 10 = 700 N.","Two rope strands through the bolt, each carries 700 N tension.","Total = 700 + 700 = 1400 N."],notesRevealed:"C5 — B♭4 — A♭4",sectionMsg:"Section IV: Summit — you've reached the peak."},
{title:"The Spiral Grove",section:"V. Forest Path",body:`<h3>🌀 LOGARITHMIC SPIRAL</h3><p>A snail shell radius multiplies by constant <em>k</em> every quarter turn. Start: <strong>1 mm</strong>. After <strong>3 full turns</strong> (12 quarter-turns): <strong>4096 mm</strong>.</p><p style="margin-top:0.8rem">What is <em>k</em>? (whole number)</p>`,answer:"2",hints:["k¹² × 1 = 4096","Which integer to the 12th power equals 4096?","2¹² = 4096. Answer: 2."],notesRevealed:"G4 — A♭4 — B♭4",sectionMsg:"Nature's mathematics, heard in the melody."},
{title:"The MTG Arena",section:"V. Forest Path",body:`<h3>🃏 MTG — THE STACK</h3><p>You control <span class="puzzle-highlight">Tarmogoyf</span>. Your graveyard: 1 Instant, 1 Sorcery, 1 Land. Opponent's: 1 Creature.</p><p style="margin-top:0.5rem"><em>Tarmogoyf = (# card types in ALL graveyards) / (same +1)</em></p><p style="margin-top:0.5rem">Opponent casts <strong>Lightning Bolt</strong>. You respond: <strong>Giant Growth</strong>. Opponent responds: <strong>Counterspell</strong> on Giant Growth.</p><p>Stack: Lightning Bolt → Giant Growth → Counterspell</p><p style="margin-top:0.8rem">After resolution: does Tarmogoyf survive? Format: <span class="puzzle-highlight">yes,N</span> or <span class="puzzle-highlight">no,N</span></p>`,answer:"yes,5",hints:["Counterspell resolves first → Giant Growth countered (goes to yard as Instant).","Now 4 types in yards → Tarmogoyf = 4/5. Lightning Bolt does 3 damage.","3 < 5 toughness → survives. Answer: yes,5"],notesRevealed:"C5 — D5 — E♭5",sectionMsg:"The stack resolves. The melody continues."},
{title:"The Regex Rune",section:"V. Forest Path",body:`<h3>💻 REGULAR EXPRESSIONS</h3><p>Pattern: <code style="color:#7ee787">^[A-Z][a-z]{2,4}[0-9]$</code></p><p>How many of these words match?</p><table><tr><th>#</th><th>Word</th><th>#</th><th>Word</th></tr><tr><td>1</td><td>Hello3</td><td>5</td><td>Z1</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td>Rx9</td><td>6</td><td>Spell2</td></tr><tr><td>3</td><td>Magic7</td><td>7</td><td>hi4</td></tr><tr><td>4</td><td>Abcd5</td><td>8</td><td>Word0</td></tr></table>`,answer:"4",hints:["Pattern: 1 uppercase + 2–4 lowercase + 1 digit.","✓Hello3, ✗Rx9(1lc), ✓Magic7, ✓Abcd5, ✗Z1(0lc), ✗Spell2(5lc), ✗hi4(lowercase start), ✓Word0","Count the ✓s: 4."],notesRevealed:"F5 — G5 — F5",sectionMsg:"Section V: Forest Path — the trees thin ahead."},
{title:"The Elevation Problem",section:"VI. The Spike",body:`<h3>🏔️ TRIGONOMETRY</h3><p>tan(30°) ≈ 0.577, tan(45°) = 1.</p><ul style="margin-left:1.5rem;line-height:2.2"><li><strong>Alpha:</strong> angle 30°, height 2000 m → horizontal distance?</li><li><strong>Gamma:</strong> angle 45°, height 3000 m → horizontal distance?</li></ul><p>Sum in <strong>whole km</strong>?</p>`,answer:"6",hints:["horizontal = height ÷ tan(angle)","Alpha: 2000÷0.577 ≈ 3464 m ≈ 3 km","Gamma: 3000÷1 = 3 km. Sum = 6 km."],notesRevealed:"A♭5 — G5 — F5",sectionMsg:"Heights calculated, melody ascending."},
{title:"The Charbelcher Problem",section:"VI. The Spike",body:`<h3>🃏 MTG — HYPERGEOMETRIC PROBABILITY</h3><p><strong>60-card deck</strong>, <strong>4 copies</strong> of <span class="puzzle-highlight">Goblin Charbelcher</span>. Mulliganed to 6 — no Charbelcher drawn. Deck: <strong>53 cards</strong>, all 4 inside.</p><p style="margin-top:0.8rem">Probability of drawing <strong>at least one</strong> in the next <strong>3 draws</strong>? (%, to 1 decimal)</p><p style="color:var(--ink-dim);font-size:0.85rem;margin-top:0.5rem">Tip: P(at least one) = 1 − P(none). P(none in 3) = (49/53) × (48/52) × (47/51)</p>`,answer:"21.4",hints:["P(at least one) = 1 − P(no Charbelcher in all 3 draws).","P(none) = (49/53)×(48/52)×(47/51).","= 110544÷140556 ≈ 0.7864. So 1−0.7864 ≈ 21.4%."],notesRevealed:"E♭5 — D5 — C5",sectionMsg:"Even chance is calculated in this quest."},
{title:"The Solstice Puzzle",section:"VI. The Spike",body:`<h3>☀️ ASTRONOMY & LOGIC</h3><p>Summer solstice in Vienna (48°N): <strong>16 hours</strong> daylight. Sunrise: <strong>04:52</strong>.</p><ul style="margin-left:1.5rem;line-height:2.2"><li>When is sunset?</li><li>Raphael hikes from <strong>06:00</strong> until <strong>30 min before sunset</strong>.</li></ul><p>Total hiking time in <strong>minutes</strong>?</p>`,answer:"862",hints:["Sunset = 04:52 + 16:00 = 20:52.","Stop time = 20:52 − 00:30 = 20:22.","20:22 − 06:00 = 14h 22min = 862 minutes."],notesRevealed:"B♭4 — C5 — D5",sectionMsg:"Section VI: The Spike — golden light at the summit."},
{title:"The Graph Labyrinth",section:"VII. The Code",body:`<h3>🕸️ GRAPH THEORY</h3><p>7 rooms. Adjacency list:</p><div class="code-block">1→2,3   2→1,4,5   3→1,6
4→2,7   5→2,6,7   6→3,5   7→4,5</div><p>How many <strong>Hamiltonian paths</strong> from Room <strong>1</strong> to Room <strong>7</strong>? (Visit every room exactly once.)</p>`,answer:"4",hints:["Start from Room 1 (go to 2 or 3). Trace systematically.","1→3→6→5→2→4→7 ✓ — one valid path.","Exhaustive search gives exactly 4 valid paths."],notesRevealed:"G5 — F5 — E♭5",sectionMsg:"Four paths through the labyrinth. Four notes."},
{title:"The Sorting Spell",section:"VII. The Code",body:`<h3>💻 ALGORITHM TRACING</h3><div class="code-block">arr = [64, 25, 12, 22, 11]
n = len(arr)
count = 0

for i in range(n-1):
    min_idx = i
    for j in range(i+1, n):
        if arr[j] &lt; arr[min_idx]:
            min_idx = j
            count += 1
    arr[min_idx], arr[i] = arr[i], arr[min_idx]

print(count)
print(arr[2])</div><p>Two numbers printed. Answer: <strong>count,arr[2]</strong></p>`,answer:"5,22",hints:["count increments each time a NEW minimum is found.","i=0: mins at j=1,2,4 (count=3). Swap 11↔64. i=1: min at j=2 (count=4). i=2: min at j=3 (count=5).","count=5, arr=[11,12,22,25,64], arr[2]=22. Answer: 5,22"],notesRevealed:"D5 — E♭5 — F5",sectionMsg:"Sorted, counted, solved."},
{title:"The Prime Fortress",section:"VII. The Code",body:`<h3>🔢 NUMBER THEORY</h3><p>Find the smallest prime <strong>p</strong> where:</p><ul style="margin-left:1.5rem;line-height:2.2"><li>p > 100</li><li>(p−1) divisible by 4</li><li>(p−2) divisible by 3</li><li>digit sum of p is also prime</li></ul>`,answer:"101",hints:["p≡1 (mod 4) and p≡2 (mod 3). Check primes above 100.","101: 101−1=100÷4=25 ✓. 101−2=99÷3=33 ✓.","Digit sum of 101 = 2, which is prime ✓. Answer: 101."],notesRevealed:"A♭5 — B♭5 — A♭5",sectionMsg:"Section VII: The Code — cracked open."},
{title:"The Final Constellation",section:"VIII. Home",body:`<h3>✨ LOGIC & STARS</h3><p>Five stars, unique brightness ranks (1=brightest). Which colour is brightest?</p><ul style="margin-left:1.5rem;line-height:2.2"><li>Red star is brighter than blue star.</li><li>Yellow star is the dimmest.</li><li>White is brighter than red but dimmer than orange.</li><li>Blue is not the dimmest.</li></ul>`,answer:"orange",hints:["Orange > White > Red > ? > Yellow (dimmest).","Blue is not dimmest → Blue between Red and Yellow.","Order: Orange(1) > White(2) > Red(3) > Blue(4) > Yellow(5). Brightest = Orange."],notesRevealed:"F5 — E♭5 — D5",sectionMsg:"The stars align. One movement remains."},
{title:"The Meta-Cipher",section:"VIII. Home",body:`<h3>🔑 THE META-PUZZLE</h3><p>Five puzzles contained a hidden number:</p><table><tr><th>Puzzle</th><th>Hidden #</th></tr><tr><td>#6 — Recursion</td><td>f(5) = <strong>5</strong></td></tr><tr><td>#13 — Spiral</td><td>k = <strong>2</strong></td></tr><tr><td>#19 — Graph</td><td>paths = <strong>4</strong></td></tr><tr><td>#22 — Constellation</td><td>rank = <strong>1</strong></td></tr><tr><td>#21 — Prime</td><td>p = <strong>101</strong></td></tr></table><p style="margin-top:0.8rem">These encode <strong>Raphael's birthday</strong>. What is the date? (DD.MM or DD/MM)</p>`,answer:"birthday",hints:["The numbers 5, 2, 4, 1, 101 are clues.","Think about when you're giving him this gift.","Type his birthday in DD.MM or DD/MM format — you definitely know this one."],notesRevealed:"B♭4 — D5 — F5 — B♭5",sectionMsg:"You remembered what matters most."},
{title:"The Last Note",section:"VIII. Home",body:`<h3>🎺 THE FINAL QUESTION</h3><p>You solved 23 puzzles. Climbed mountains, cast spells, traced code, mapped stars, navigated labyrinths.</p><p style="margin-top:1.2rem;font-size:1.2rem;color:var(--gold);text-align:center;line-height:2">"What is the thing that makes<br/>a melody more than just notes?"</p><p style="margin-top:1.2rem;text-align:center;color:var(--ink-dim)">One word:<br/><em style="color:var(--ink)">A melody becomes music when it carries _______.</em></p>`,answer:"heart",hints:["Not technique, timing, or theory.","It's what makes you play differently for a friend than a stranger.","Love, soul, feeling — the simplest word for all of them: heart."],notesRevealed:"B♭4 — F5 — B♭5 — D6 — B♭5 — F5 — B♭4",sectionMsg:"🎺 The composition is complete. Happy Birthday, Raphael."}
];



